					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13893018</guid>
				<title>SCP-5217</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13893018/scp-5217</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 02 Dec 2020 22:27:56 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>stormmageexpert</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>7003081</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I had this idea in July when I read <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1423">SCP-1423</a> and saw a photo a former classmate posted on the same day (not the one in the article, for licensing reasons). It just wouldn't get out of my head, so I decided to flesh it out fully, then to work to make it unique, then to put it in Wikidot format in a sandbox. Figured I might as well cold-post it and see if it sinks or swims.</p> <p>I don't know if this story continues or not, but if it does, I'm sure that it happens in the Academics version of <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/war-on-all-fronts-hub">War on All Fronts</a>. But this won't even survive 24 hours so it's pretty silly to think that'll happen.</p> <p>Lots of people to thank, first among them my friend Alice for drawing the sketch at the end. Next up is <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rjb-r" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1229263&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606958715" alt="RJB_R" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1229263)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rjb-r" >RJB_R</a></span> for writing the SCP that inspired this, even if it has evolved quite a bit since then. Then <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/qntm" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=571081&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606958715" alt="qntm" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=571081)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/qntm" >qntm</a></span>, who gets a shoutout through Site 41 in the article, for being so dang cool. Also thanks to the people who made the Wiki Syntax guide (I stole all your code no regrets!) and the people who wrote the How to Write an SCP guide for saying that sentient beings have to be Euclid and Foundation personnel aren't stupid. Breaking rules is fun if you're clever about it and don't care about the result!</p> <p>Have a great day and a great life, and if you upvote, a good month as well!</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
